
dsh-video-channel
=================

This project is a fork of dsh-video-vision
(https://github.com/Destinhue/dsh-video-vision), which is MIT licensed.
The upstream work — frame extraction, cut detection, storyboard compositing, zoom,
video probing, text reading — is theirs and is reused here unchanged except for the
two files listed in patches/DIFF.md.

What was added on top:

  · src/longform.js      a whole-episode channel: dedupe pictures by frame change,
                         OCR every second of burned-in subtitles, emit [second] lines
  · video_scan           exposes that channel as a tool
  · video_where          maps a subtitle line back to a storyboard cell, so a face can
                         be looked at with video_zoom instead of guessed from a small cell

Why the package was renamed: keeping the upstream name would mean anyone who installed
this fork stops receiving upstream updates (same package name, one overwrites the other).
Under its own name this can sit next to dsh-video-vision, or replace it — it is a superset.

